# PART 3 — PRIMARY ARCHITECTURAL REQUIREMENT

Implement the following data-authority model using the existing Firebase architecture.

## 3.1 Cloud Firestore is the authoritative source

Every finalized attendance record must be stored in the correct existing Cloud Firestore document.

The authoritative record must contain, or reliably reference, all information required to reconstruct the class card after reopening the website:

- Student identity.
- Scheduled session/class identity.
- AttendWise attendance status.
- ERP attendance status.
- Keynote/reason text.
- Photo evidence reference or stored evidence, according to the existing architecture.
- Relevant timestamps.
- Finalization state and any other existing fields needed by application rules.
- Existing metadata required for history, analytics, and synchronization.

Do not create a second competing database or a separate cache that acts as the source of truth.

Before making changes, discover the actual existing collection names, document IDs, field names, and nested structure. Reuse the existing schema wherever possible. Do not invent new paths and leave old code reading from the previous paths.

If the existing schema contains a confirmed defect that prevents correct persistence, make the smallest compatible correction and provide a safe migration strategy only if a migration is genuinely necessary.

## 3.2 Local browser state must never be the only copy

Inspect React state, context, hooks, localStorage, sessionStorage, IndexedDB, and Firestore's offline persistence configuration.

These mechanisms may be useful for UI state or offline functionality, but they must not be mistaken for successful cloud persistence.

Specifically:

- React state may render the current attendance card.
- Local storage may support non-authoritative preferences or recovery of an unsaved draft where appropriate.
- IndexedDB or Firestore's persistent cache may be used if compatible with the current Firebase setup.
- None of these mechanisms may silently substitute a locally cached status for a required, cloud-confirmed record.
- Browser storage must not determine a new student identity on every visit.
- Clearing or losing browser storage must not erase the authoritative attendance record.
- Do not remove all caching indiscriminately. First determine which cache is used and whether it causes the actual defect.

The system must recover its records from Firebase even when the browser has no previous local attendance state.

